  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 118 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nAs of 115 PM Monday afternoon, quasi-zonal midlevel flow remains \nacross much of the CONUS with a weak shortwave trough across north \nTX and across the upper MS valley. A weak surface trough extends \nfrom northern MN through northwest KS. Limited cold air resides \nwithin the post-frontal airmass with 70s ahead of the front and \nupper 60s behind. This frontal passage will sweep across the entire \narea overnight with a weak area of surface high pressure settling \ninto the region for Tuesday. This should yield light winds and \ntemperatures similar to today. \n\nThe next shortwave trough is poised to eject into the Plains late \nTuesday night into Wednesday. This will shunt another cold front \nthrough the forecast area Wednesday. Temperatures behind the front \nwill be noticeable cooler with highs by Thursday in the 50s to near \n60. These closer to normal temperatures in the 50s and 60s will \ncontinue into the upcoming weekend. The chance for rainfall may \narrive late in the weekend as a western CONUS trough advances toward \nthe central Plains on Sunday.",
